WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.734
At a high level, the brain and nervous system are made of cells and networks that communicate through patterns of activity.

2
00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:17.053
Neurons connect with other neurons, and those connections participate in pathways that support perception, movement, thought, memory, emotion, and action.

3
00:00:17.053 --> 00:00:22.876
For this course, the practical point is that learning is not just receiving information.

4
00:00:22.876 --> 00:00:27.035
It involves changes in how patterns are activated and used.

5
00:00:27.035 --> 00:00:30.778
Patterns can be strengthened or weakened through repeated use.

6
00:00:30.778 --> 00:00:37.017
A skill that is practiced often, with attention and feedback, can become easier to access.

7
00:00:37.017 --> 00:00:42.840
A behavior that is repeatedly triggered by the same cue can become more automatic.

8
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.583
A strategy that is rarely used may remain effortful.

9
00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:54.901
This is often described as use-dependent change: the nervous system adapts partly in response to what is repeatedly used.

10
00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:58.645
Attention, emotion, repetition, feedback, and context all influence learning.

11
00:00:58.645 --> 00:01:01.140
Attention helps select what is processed.

12
00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:05.299
Repetition gives the system multiple chances to stabilize a pattern.

13
00:01:05.299 --> 00:01:07.379
Feedback helps correct the pattern.

14
00:01:07.379 --> 00:01:13.202
Context provides cues that tell the learner when and how to use the skill.

15
00:01:13.202 --> 00:01:19.857
Emotion and relevance can influence whether an experience receives enough priority to be remembered and revisited.

16
00:01:19.857 --> 00:01:24.848
The practical implication is clear: people adapt to the systems around them.

17
00:01:24.848 --> 00:01:29.423
Training, routines, incentives, tools, and environments all shape what gets repeated.

18
00:01:29.423 --> 00:01:33.998
If a workplace rewards rushed work, rushed patterns may become normal.

19
00:01:33.998 --> 00:01:40.237
If a learning design rewards retrieval, correction, and reflection, those patterns become easier to use.

20
00:01:40.237 --> 00:01:46.060
Behavior design is not separate from learning; it is part of the learning environment.
